From 5594ae1e3fd6727ac910cafb651316f7549cadb1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Janota <Roman.Janota@cesnet.cz>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 18:03:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] notifd FEATURE yang-push periodic subscriptions

Configured RFC 8641 datastore subscriptions with a periodic update
trigger. The datastore target is parsed with its selection filter, by
reference or within the subscription, a subtree one converted into the
node set it selects. Every resubscription parses the target and the
update policy again from the stored subscription, so any change of the
stream or datastore target or of the update policy just resubscribes.
That replaces the per-leaf handlers of the stream target, and a switch
of the target case needs no special handling. A named filter is read
like one within the subscription, so an empty stream subtree filter
means no filter in both.

The validation rejects a datastore without a sysrepo counterpart, a
subscription without an update trigger, a period of 0 or one that does
not fit in milliseconds, and a selection filter, also a named one,
with nodes that do not exist or an empty subtree, which would silently
select nothing (RFC 8641 section 3.9 allows the rejection). The state
change notifications report the datastore target and the update
policy. The generated records are left to SRSN, the dispatch loop only
sets the configured subscription ID in the ietf-yang-push records of a
datastore subscription.

ietf-yang-push stays optional for the daemon, setup_notifd.sh installs
it with on-change.

Upstream: https://github.com/sysrepo/sysrepo/commit/20e756e510a558d3a499615b2272aa0c928b9aa8
Signed-off-by: Mattias Walström <lazzer@gmail.com>
